.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt PAZARID 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pazarid
.Nd host memory daemon for pazari
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Nm
.Cm example-config
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs on a virtualisation host.
It accepts connections from
.Xr pazari-agent 1
in each guest, decides whether a guest may grow, and carries out grants by
resizing the guest's virtio-mem device over QMP.
When configured to, it asks guests to return memory while the host is under
memory pressure.
.Pp
The daemon keeps no persistent state.
Guests are defined in its configuration file, and everything else is read from
.Pa /proc
and the hypervisor.
After a restart, guests reconnect and report their state again.
.Pp
With no command,
.Nm
runs in the foreground until it receives
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT .
It reads its configuration once, at startup.
.Ss Grants
A grow is granted if the host's available memory, less memory already promised
to other guests and less the growth requested, is at least
.Cm grant.floor .
Available memory is
.Va MemAvailable ,
plus
.Va SwapFree
if
.Cm grant.swap
is set.
Grants are capped at the guest's ceiling and may be smaller than requested.
.Pp
A refusal gives one of these reasons, which the guest receives:
.Bl -tag -width "host_pressure"
.It Cm ceiling
The guest is less than one of its memory blocks below its ceiling.
Retrying will not help until the ceiling is raised.
.It Cm host_pressure
The host does not have the memory, or has not yet read its memory figures.
The guest is told to retry after
.Cm grant.min_interval .
.It Cm rate_limited
The guest was granted memory less than
.Cm grant.min_interval
ago.
The guest is told how long to wait.
.It Cm policy
The guest is unknown, or its memory device has not yet reported a size.
.El
.Pp
Offers to release memory are always accepted.
.Ss Reclaim
The daemon never removes memory from a guest.
With
.Cm reclaim.revocation
configured, it asks guests to return memory while the host is under pressure,
and a guest may refuse; see
.Xr pazarid.toml 5 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar file , Fl -config Ar file
Read the configuration from
.Ar file
instead of
.Pa /etc/pazari/pazarid.toml .
May appear before or after a command.
.It Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm example-config
Print an annotated configuration file with every key at its default.
.El
.Sh STARTUP
At startup the daemon:
.Bl -enum
.It
Reads
.Pa /proc/meminfo ,
and exits if it cannot.
.It
Warns if the guests' ceilings plus
.Cm grant.floor
exceed the host's RAM plus swap.
See
.Sx CAPACITY
in
.Xr pazarid.toml 5 .
.It
Exits if
.Cm reclaim.revocation
is configured and the kernel does not provide
.Pa /proc/pressure/memory .
.It
Warns if
.Cm grant.swap
is set and the host swaps to zram.
.It
Connects to each guest's QMP socket, opens its listeners, and reports
readiness to systemd.
.El
.Pp
A QMP socket that does not exist yet is retried with backoff, so the daemon and
its virtual machines may start in any order.
.Sh PRIVILEGE
The daemon needs no capabilities.
It must be able to connect to each guest's QMP socket, which is usually granted
by group membership.
vsock ports 1023 and below require
.Dv CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE .
.Pp
QMP gives full control of the hypervisor.
Give the daemon its own QMP socket rather than sharing the VM manager's; see
.Xr pazari 7 .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev RUST_LOG
Log filter, in
.Va tracing-subscriber
.Va EnvFilter
syntax.
Defaults to
.Cm info .
.It Ev JOURNAL_STREAM
Set by systemd.
When it refers to the daemon's standard error, the daemon logs to the journal
directly, with structured fields prefixed
.Cm F_ .
.It Ev NOTIFY_SOCKET
Set by systemd for
.Va Type=notify .
The daemon reports readiness and sends watchdog pings here.
.It Ev WATCHDOG_USEC
Watchdog interval.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/pazari/pazarid.toml
Default configuration file; see
.Xr pazarid.toml 5 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate a configuration file to edit:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# pazarid example-config > /etc/pazari/pazarid.toml
.Ed
.Pp
Check guest sizes, available memory and refusals without Prometheus:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9650/ | grep -E 'guest_size|host_available|denies'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pazari-agent 1 ,
.Xr pazari-stress 1 ,
.Xr qemu 1 ,
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 ,
.Xr pazarid.toml 5 ,
.Xr proc 5 ,
.Xr pazari 7
